Using 3.4.3 on Linux with Hearse, I recently came across several bones
piles (none of them my own) all of which contained one or more "end
users". These items were classified as comestibles. Also, the bones
(maybe three different piles spread across two or three levels) all had
different names (i.e., perhaps not the same user(?)).

Anyway, I couldn't find anything about an "end user" on Wikihack,
in a broader Google search, or in a search of the RGRN Google Groups archive. 

For the record, the item in inventory was "an end user", not "an end
user corpse".

Is this just someone playing with creative item names or what (do item
names even "survive" in bones)?

